  "text": "4.4 One other animal that is as at home in the city as in the countryside is the raccoon. In fact, raccoons are so at home in the city that the number of city raccoons has increased. Raccoons have different diets depending on their environment. Common foods include fruit, plants, nuts and rodents. Much like the foxes of London, raccoons living in the city are known to eat rubbish out of bins, steal food from people's homes and occasionally bite people.",
